        "answer": "# Newton's Second Law\n\nNewton's second law of motion states that the rate of change of momentum of an object is directly proportional to the applied unbalanced force in the direction of the force.\n\nMathematically, it is expressed as:\n$F = ma$\n\nWhere:\n*   **F** = net external force acting on the object (in Newtons)\n*   **m** = mass of the object (in kg)\n*   **a** = acceleration of the object (in m/s²)\n\nThis law provides a method to measure the force acting on an object as a product of its mass and acceleration . It applies when there is a net external force acting on a body .\n\n**📘 Source:** NCERT Class 9 Science • Newton Second Law"
